                                "sense_id": "dc5d2ea1-2d1a-3dc7-a557-cfe7eca44c8f",
                                "text": "\"I beg your pardon,\" said Egremont blushing; \"I was reading your name. I thought I was reading it to myself. Sybil Gerard! What a beautiful name is Sybil!\" \"My mother's name,\" said Gerard; \"and my grandame's name, and a name I believe that has been about our hearth as long as our race; and that's a very long time indeed,\" he added smiling, \"for we were tall men in King John's reign, as I have heard say.\""
